<title>USA: CVS offering little premium for Revco - WSJ.</title>
<headline>CVS offering little premium for Revco - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>CVS Corp has proposed an all-stock deal to acquire Revco D.S. Inc that would give Revco holders little or no premium, the Wall Street Journal said Tuesday.</p>
<p>People familiar with the talks said the negotiations involved a price range of about $38 to $40 for each Revco share, but also say the price may change, the paper said.</p>
<p>Revco shares closed Monday at 38-7/8.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
